<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<WorkflowBuilder Version="2.9.0"
                 xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                 xmlns:rx="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Reactive;assembly=Bonsai.Core"
                 xmlns:aud="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Audio;assembly=OpenRigs.Audio"
                 xmlns="https://bonsai-rx.org/2018/workflow">
  <Description>A task's background noise, the same file and level in every task: rig.yml's speakerArray.backgroundNoise (relative to rig.yml's folder, ../shared/sounds/background_noise.wav, the server's config\shared copy, kept on the rig by its upkeep), read whole at Start with the speakers (ReadBackgroundNoise, which stops, naming the file, when rig.yml names none, it is missing, or it is not at speakerArray.device.sampleRate, as nothing converts a rate), laid out as it is on every rig.yml speaker (SpeakerBuffer, not equalised) at the lab's -60 dBFS RMS (SoundLevel.BackgroundDbfs; no task setting), and sent into SpeakerMixer's BackgroundNoise at Ready, which loops it, faded in over 2 s. Subjects: Speakers, Ready.</Description>
  <Workflow>
    <Nodes>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>Speakers</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="aud:ReadBackgroundNoise" />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>Speakers</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="aud:SpeakerBuffer">
          <aud:Channels />
          <aud:LevelDbfs>-60</aud:LevelDbfs>
          <aud:Equalise>false</aud:Equalise>
          <aud:SyncCopy>false</aud:SyncCopy>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>Ready</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
        <Selector>Item1</Selector>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
        <Name>BackgroundNoise</Name>
      </Expression>
    </Nodes>
    <Edges>
      <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="1" To="3" Label="Source2" />
      <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="4" To="6" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source2" />
      <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
    </Edges>
  </Workflow>
</WorkflowBuilder>
